WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:21.673
The sun was just beginning to peek into the windows of our apartment at 221B Baker Street when

2
00:00:21.713 --> 00:00:26.154
the lady of Stoke Moran finished her terrible story about the death of her twin sister.

3
00:00:26.174 --> 00:00:30.276
"If I may," my friend and associate Mr.

4
00:00:30.316 --> 00:00:35.946
Sherlock Holmes asked, "I would like to make sure of some of the details before I begin my

5
00:00:36.026 --> 00:00:42.008
investigation. Now, you mentioned there was a whistling sound followed by a clang of metal.

6
00:00:42.728 --> 00:00:44.869
Are you sure this is what you heard that night?"

7
00:00:44.889 --> 00:00:48.371
"I will never forget it," responded Miss Stoner.

8
00:00:48.391 --> 00:00:55.073
"It was an odd whistle that sounded like a strange melody, followed by a harsh metallic clang."

9
00:00:56.054 --> 00:00:58.215
"Did you explain these events to the coroner?"

10
00:00:58.895 --> 00:00:59.655
inquired Holmes.

11
00:01:01.708 --> 00:01:06.432
"Of course, but even after a thorough examination of her body, he was still unable to determine the

12
00:01:06.472 --> 00:01:07.192
cause of death.

13
00:01:07.993 --> 00:01:11.055
There were no signs of violence and no evidence of poison.

14
00:01:12.116 --> 00:01:17.140
Mr. Holmes, you may think I am silly, but I believe that my sister died of fright.

15
00:01:18.001 --> 00:01:19.963
She was white as a ghost when I found her.

16
00:01:20.603 --> 00:01:23.325
Something terrible must have roused her from her bed."

17
00:01:24.146 --> 00:01:28.469
It was then that I remembered the guests in the woods behind the house and spoke up.

18
00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:30.611
"Do you think it was the Gypsies?"

19
00:01:31.211 --> 00:01:31.612
I asked.

20
00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.200
Miss Stoner nodded.

21
00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:36.681
"The Gypsy women often wear handkerchiefs over their hair.

22
00:01:37.461 --> 00:01:40.742
Perhaps this is what Julia meant by ‘the speckled band.'"

23
00:01:41.623 --> 00:01:46.664
I wrote down this evidence in my leather notebook and glanced over at Holmes, who was now sitting

24
00:01:46.704 --> 00:01:48.884
with his head tilted back and his eyes closed.

25
00:01:49.645 --> 00:01:52.105
He did this only when he was deep in thought.

26
00:01:52.125 --> 00:01:54.966
"What is the situation at Stoke Moran now?"

27
00:01:55.466 --> 00:01:59.767
I asked, hoping this would encourage Miss Stoner to reveal more facts about the case.

28
00:02:00.668 --> 00:02:03.668
"That is why I am here," explained the young woman.

29
00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:07.689
Holmes appeared to perk up at this statement and opened his eyes.

30
00:02:07.709 --> 00:02:10.230
"Continue, please," he said.

31
00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.131
Miss Stoner avoided eye contact with Holmes.

32
00:02:13.751 --> 00:02:16.532
Instead she stared sadly down at the floor.

33
00:02:17.392 --> 00:02:22.074
She became slightly more agitated, and a shudder of terror seemed to ripple through her before she spoke.

34
00:02:22.094 --> 00:02:27.095
"As I told you," she said, "it's been two years since Julia's death.

35
00:02:27.935 --> 00:02:32.176
Last summer, when I was the loneliest I have ever been, my dear friend Mr.

36
00:02:32.336 --> 00:02:36.538
Percy Armitage of Crane Water did me the honor of asking for my hand in marriage.

37
00:02:37.358 --> 00:02:40.519
With no objection from my stepfather, I graciously accepted.

38
00:02:41.139 --> 00:02:43.059
The two of us plan to wed next month."

39
00:02:43.699 --> 00:02:45.920
"Congratulations!" I interrupted.

40
00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.680
"You must be very happy."

41
00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:53.282
"I would be," she explained, "except there have been some very frightful events."

42
00:02:54.222 --> 00:02:59.023
At this comment Holmes leaned forward in a position I knew signaled great interest.

43
00:03:00.124 --> 00:03:03.350
"Last week," Miss Stoner continued, "Dr.

44
00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:06.993
Roylott informed me that he would be making some renovations in the house.

45
00:03:07.914 --> 00:03:11.076
He told me I would need to move from my own room at the end of the hall

46
00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:13.198
into Julia's old room, next to his own.

47
00:03:14.079 --> 00:03:19.864
I was surprised to hear this—we have not done repairs in quite some time—but I moved my things

48
00:03:19.984 --> 00:03:20.684
as requested.

49
00:03:21.445 --> 00:03:23.867
It has been awful trying to sleep in Julia's room!

50
00:03:24.648 --> 00:03:29.672
I either lie awake all night or suffer horrible nightmares when I do manage to fall asleep.

51
00:03:30.516 --> 00:03:33.717
Last evening, however, something terrifying happened.

52
00:03:34.537 --> 00:03:39.098
I heard a whistling sound—the same one I remember from the night Julia died!

53
00:03:39.779 --> 00:03:41.939
That is why I have contacted you, Mr.

54
00:03:41.979 --> 00:03:44.960
Holmes. I believe I am in grave danger."

55
00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:49.321
"This is a serious case, Miss Stoner," Holmes agreed.

56
00:03:50.161 --> 00:03:54.943
Then he pointed to her arms and said, "But you are also hiding something."

57
00:03:55.983 --> 00:04:01.481
Miss Stoner moved her arms in a way that caused her sleeves to slip upward, revealing several large

58
00:04:01.521 --> 00:04:02.822
bruises on her forearms.

59
00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.124
"Yes," she said.

60
00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:10.568
"When I informed my stepfather that I was having trouble sleeping and wished to move out of Julia's

61
00:04:10.628 --> 00:04:15.112
room, he grabbed me hard and demanded that I stay until the repairs are complete.

62
00:04:15.813 --> 00:04:17.514
Do you think that you can help me?"

63
00:04:18.335 --> 00:04:23.679
Holmes immediately offered his assistance but explained to our new client that he would first need to gather

64
00:04:23.719 --> 00:04:25.020
a good deal of information.

65
00:04:25.792 --> 00:04:29.474
He then asked if it would be possible for the two of us to examine the rooms at

66
00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:30.954
Stoke Moran without Dr.

67
00:04:30.994 --> 00:04:31.775
Roylott's knowledge.

68
00:04:31.795 --> 00:04:35.276
"He will be out of the house today," Miss Stoner said.

69
00:04:35.296 --> 00:04:40.198
"He is running errands in town and will not be home until after the supper hour."

70
00:04:40.919 --> 00:04:44.400
Holmes made plans to meet the young woman at Stoke Moran that afternoon.

71
00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:49.382
Appearing relieved to have acquired our help, she said good-bye and left.

72
00:04:49.402 --> 00:04:53.424
"A most interesting case indeed," I said aloud.

73
00:04:54.208 --> 00:04:58.651
Holmes, who had failed to nod in agreement, was already gathering his things to begin his research.

74
00:04:59.451 --> 00:05:00.872
Where are you going, my good fellow?"

75
00:05:01.612 --> 00:05:05.335
I asked, quite surprised that he was so hasty in his preparations.

76
00:05:05.355 --> 00:05:10.878
"I have some research to complete before we travel to Stoke Moran," Holmes replied.

77
00:05:10.898 --> 00:05:15.521
"Oh, but I suppose I should not assume that you will be joining me on the adventure.

78
00:05:16.241 --> 00:05:17.121
It will be dangerous."

79
00:05:18.062 --> 00:05:19.203
"I most definitely will!"

80
00:05:19.963 --> 00:05:21.204
I responded without delay.

81
00:05:22.036 --> 00:05:27.299
"But I simply cannot understand what is happening to Miss Stoner and what killed her dear sister.

82
00:05:27.879 --> 00:05:32.262
The evidence is confusing I was hoping that Holmes would enlighten me.

83
00:05:32.982 --> 00:05:37.885
But before he had a chance to respond, the front door to the apartment swung open wildly and

84
00:05:37.945 --> 00:05:39.465
a tall figure marched through.

85
00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:44.348
In an angry voice, the stranger proclaimed, "I am Dr.

86
00:05:44.408 --> 00:05:48.290
Grimesby Roylott, and I have followed my stepdaughter to your apartment.

87
00:05:49.411 --> 00:05:51.532
I demand to know who you two are!"

88
00:05:52.488 --> 00:05:53.849
"This is my colleague, Dr.

89
00:05:53.889 --> 00:05:55.310
Watson, and I am Mr.

90
00:05:55.371 --> 00:06:00.575
Sherlock Holmes," answered my associate as he put out his hand to greet the unwelcome guest.

91
00:06:01.335 --> 00:06:03.637
Roylott, however, ignored the polite gesture.

92
00:06:04.198 --> 00:06:08.161
He moved quickly to the fireplace and picked up the metal poker that was lying on the mantel.

93
00:06:08.181 --> 00:06:10.283
"The famous detective?

94
00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:16.688
Well, my good man, I don't want you meddling in my affairs," Roylott said threateningly.

95
00:06:17.628 --> 00:06:22.231
Then, much to my surprise, he took the poker in both hands and, with incredible strength, bent it

96
00:06:22.271 --> 00:06:22.652
in half.

97
00:06:22.672 --> 00:06:24.953
"Do I make myself clear?"

98
00:06:25.594 --> 00:06:26.794
Holmes did not respond.

99
00:06:27.355 --> 00:06:31.778
He merely pulled back his outstretched hand and placed it into the right pocket of his vest.

100
00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:37.402
As he did this, I moved closer to him in case the situation erupted into a fight.

101
00:06:38.162 --> 00:06:43.666
Holmes, of course, was a competent boxer; nevertheless, I wanted to show my loyalty to him.

102
00:06:44.526 --> 00:06:46.748
I did not appreciate such bullying in our home.

103
00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:53.506
My protection, however, wasn't necessary because Roylott quickly spun around and marched out the door with the same

104
00:06:53.766 --> 00:06:55.628
anger in his step as when he arrived.

105
00:06:56.228 --> 00:06:58.510
I rushed over and bolted the door shut behind him.

106
00:06:59.291 --> 00:07:02.434
"What a pleasant gentleman," said Holmes sarcastically.

107
00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:08.579
Then he walked over to the fireplace, picked up the poker, and easily bent it back into shape.

108
00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:14.904
He placed it back on the mantel, retrieved his briefcase from the bedroom, and announced, "I am going

109
00:07:14.964 --> 00:07:19.506
to the hospital library to do some research and will be back in time to meet with you

110
00:07:19.566 --> 00:07:21.227
before we leave for Stoke Moran.

111
00:07:21.987 --> 00:07:24.989
Pack your bag, Watson, and don't forget to bring your pistol.

112
00:07:25.549 --> 00:07:27.570
It looks as if we may require it today."
